# Milestone: v0.10.10-job-introspection
# Covers: no strand leak after a block containing '&'-joined strands; Job.jobs
#         count returns to baseline after completion.
# matrix-row: scheduler-jobs
#
# Rewritten from legacy tests/2.x/jobs-destruction.chk for the host
# driver.  `Job.jobs` is a method here, so the count is
# `Job.jobs().size()`; integer ranges are not iterable, so the ten
# rounds are a `while`.  The control first proves the count sees a live
# strand -- a detached sleeper raises it, and it drops back once the
# sleeper is woken and reaped -- so the baseline comparison after the
# `&` rounds can fail.
## timeout: 30
## host: run var njobs = Job.jobs().size()
## host: run { sleep(1s) }, 0
## host: step 1000
## host: run Job.jobs().size() == njobs + 1
## host: advance-clock 1000
## host: step 1000
## host: run Job.jobs().size() == njobs
## host: run { var i = 0; while (i < 10) { 1 & 2 & 3; i = i + 1 } }, 0
## host: step 1000
## host: run Job.jobs().size() == njobs
[00000000] 1
[00000000] 0
[00000000] step: WAKE_AT
[00000000] true
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] true
[00000000] 0
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] true
